      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 1,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to play Ash Barrens as their land for turn 2, missing a land drop for no reason. They have Cultivate in hand needing 3 mana, and already have two Forests in hand for future turns, so there's no benefit to holding Ash Barrens.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without playing a land on turn 2.",
      "better_line": "Play Ash Barrens as the land drop to have 2 lands on board, enabling Cultivate on turn 3 after playing a Forest.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 13,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 13,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to play Ash Barrens when it was offered as a legal play. Even as a colorless source, having 2 lands on turn 2 is significantly better than 1 land, accelerating toward casting Cultivate and Orazca Frillback. With only 1 Forest on board and expensive cards in hand (Cultivate at 3, Frillback at 3, Ghalta at 12), every land drop matters.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without playing Ash Barrens",
      "better_line": "Play Ash Barrens to have 2 mana sources available, enabling faster development toward Cultivate on turn 3 (with a Forest play) or at minimum having more mana available sooner.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 15,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 15,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Kimi25 Tactic has Thieves' Guild Enforcer available to cast at instant speed during combat (before blockers), with 1 Black mana available from the untapped Swamp. Casting it here would mill the opponent 2 cards (getting closer to the 8-card graveyard threshold for the +2/+1 and deathtouch bonus), and importantly, it has flash so there's no downside to deploying it now rather than later. The player passed on the only available action, declining a free opportunity to develop the board and advance their mill gameplan.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting Thieves' Guild Enforcer",
      "better_line": "Cast Thieves' Guild Enforcer for {B} during combat. This develops a creature, mills the opponent 2 cards, and preserves the option to block or attack next turn. There is no reason to hold it since there are no other instant-speed plays competing for that mana this turn cycle (Sentinels costs 4, Undersea Invader costs 6).",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 52,
      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 47,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Cultivate before playing a Forest from hand. Should play the land first to maximize available mana before committing to a spell. Playing land first means having an extra untapped land available during the resolution and afterward, which is strictly better.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Cultivate without first making the available land drop",
      "better_line": "Play Forest from hand first, then cast Cultivate with the additional mana available",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 61,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 56,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Unnatural Aggression before playing a land drop. With 5 untapped Forests and only needing {2}{G}, the mana was sufficient, but playing a land first (Forest or Thriving Grove) is free and preserves options. More importantly, if the player fights the Frillback into Cutthroat, the Frillback dies (5 power vs 3/2, but Frillback only has 2 toughness and takes 3 back), losing the Frillback + Setessan Training + Unnatural Aggression for just the Cutthroat. Using Drover (3/3, tapped but can still fight) would be much better as the target.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Unnatural Aggression before playing a land drop and before selecting fight targets.",
      "better_line": "Play a land first (Thriving Grove for color fixing), then cast Unnatural Aggression targeting Drover of the Mighty to fight Brineborn Cutthroat, preserving the more valuable Orazca Frillback with trample.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 137,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 105,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Fighting Brineborn Cutthroat (3/2) with Orazca Frillback (6/2 with Setessan Training) means the Frillback takes 3 damage and dies (only 2 toughness). Fighting Oona's Blackguard (1/1) instead would kill the Blackguard while the Frillback survives with only 1 damage taken. Oona's Blackguard is also a key synergy piece that gives +1/+1 counters to entering Rogues and enables discard, making it a high-value target. Removing it while keeping the 6/2 trampler alive is clearly superior.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Brineborn Cutthroat with Unnatural Aggression, causing the Frillback to die in the fight",
      "better_line": "Target Oona's Blackguard with Unnatural Aggression - the Frillback survives the fight (takes only 1 damage vs 2 toughness), removes a dangerous synergy piece, and keeps the 6-power trampler on board for attacking",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 139,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 107,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed on flashing in Sentinels of Glen Elendra while Oona's Blackguard is on the battlefield. Sentinels is a Rogue, so it would enter with an additional +1/+1 counter (becoming a 3/4 flyer) and would trigger Thieves' Guild Enforcer's mill ability. The +1/+1 counter also means combat damage triggers Oona's Blackguard's discard ability. This represents significant value and board pressure against an opponent at 10 life.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, declining to cast Sentinels of Glen Elendra",
      "better_line": "Cast Sentinels of Glen Elendra for {3}{U} to get a 3/4 flying Rogue with discard synergy from Oona's Blackguard, plus mill 2 from Thieves' Guild Enforcer trigger",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 169,
      "player": "Kimi25 Tactic",
      "decision_index": 130,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 10 life facing 6 damage from attackers (3 from deathtouch Enforcer + 2 from flying Sentinels + 1 from flying Blackguard), going to 4 life is extremely dangerous since opponent has multiple flyers that threaten lethal next turn. Blocking Thieves' Guild Enforcer with Drowsing Tyrannodon would trade the Tyrannodon (less valuable, summoning sick) but save 3 life, going to 7 instead of 4. At 4 life, opponent's flyers (Sentinels 2/3, Blackguard 1/1, Nightshade Stinger 2/2) deal 5 flying damage next turn which is lethal.",
      "action_taken": "No response/timeout - did not declare any blockers, taking full 6 damage to drop to 4 life.",
      "better_line": "Block Thieves' Guild Enforcer with Drowsing Tyrannodon. The Tyrannodon trades due to deathtouch but saves 3 life, going to 7 instead of 4, which survives the opponent's next flying attack and gives more time to win with Ghalta.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 218,
      "player": "Grk41F Timmy",
      "decision_index": 160,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
